# Start the backend first; change the port here if needed.
# Run individual requests with an HTTP client that supports .http files.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### Welcome message: 200 with the backend welcome message
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### Liveness: 200 with status, service, version, and Cache-Control: no-store
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### Headers-only liveness: 200 with no body and a new X-Request-ID
HEAD {{baseUrl}}/health

### API contract: 200 with the generated OpenAPI schema
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.json
Accept: application/json

### Unknown route: 404 with a detail field and X-Request-ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/missing
Accept: application/json

### Unsupported health write: 405 with a detail field and X-Request-ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### Consultation directory: 200 with nine fictional listings ordered by ID.
### Needs PostgreSQL migrated and seeded; see the README.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/consultations
Accept: application/json

### Search: every term must match name, specialty or area (c-01 and c-06)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/consultations?q=riverside%20clinic
Accept: application/json

### "Up to ₹300": free examples plus known fees up to 30000 paise (c-01, c-02, c-03, c-08)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/consultations?max_fee_minor=30000
Accept: application/json

### Explicit free only (c-03, c-08)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/consultations?fee_state=free
Accept: application/json

### Fee not listed (c-06, c-09)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/consultations?fee_state=unknown
Accept: application/json

### Combined filters (c-09)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/consultations?specialty=Dermatology&mode=video&fee_state=unknown
Accept: application/json

### No matches: 200 with an empty items list and total 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/consultations?q=no-such-provider
Accept: application/json

### Invalid filter: 422 with a detail list naming the query parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/consultations?mode=fax
Accept: application/json

# With PostgreSQL stopped or MEDASSIST_DATABASE_URL unset, the directory
# returns 503 with a generic detail and request_id; /health still returns 200.
